        "original_id": "97d818bf-04e2-55d9-878f-38962fc7d4c3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: State Theatre, Arts Centre Melbourne, Southbank, Yarra River, St Kilda Road, Melbourne Arts Precinct, Victoria, Australia\n- Organizations: Arts Centre Melbourne, Victorian Arts Centre\n- Events: State Theatre opening, Shout! The Legend of The Wild One premiere\n- Works: Shout! The Legend of The Wild One\n\nFacts:\n- The State Theatre in Melbourne opened in 1984.\n- The State Theatre is part of Arts Centre Melbourne and is located by the Yarra River and St Kilda Road.\n- Arts Centre Melbourne was originally known as the Victorian Arts Centre and was briefly officially called the Arts Centre.\n- Arts Centre Melbourne is a performing arts centre made up of theatres and concert halls in the Melbourne Arts Precinct in Southbank, Victoria, Australia.\n- Shout! The Legend of The Wild One premiered at the State Theatre in Melbourne in December 2000.\n- Shout! The Legend of The Wild One then had seasons in Sydney, Adelaide, and Brisbane through 2001.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
