        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a4c8d2c6-bd70-5603-80e5-abe24b21f1f5",
        "text": "Page: State Theatre (Melbourne). Sentence: The State Theatre opened in 1984 and is part of the Arts Centre Melbourne located by the Yarra River and St Kilda Road.\nPage: Arts Centre Melbourne. Sentence: The Arts Centre Melbourne, originally known as the Victorian Arts Centre and briefly officially called the Arts Centre, is a performing arts centre consisting of a complex of theatres and concert halls in the Melbourne Arts Precinct, located in the central Melbourne suburb of Southbank in Victoria, Australia.\nPage: Shout! The Legend of The Wild One. Sentence: It premiered in Melbourne at the State Theatre in December 2000, before seasons in Sydney, Adelaide and Brisbane through 2001.",
